      "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;The company behind the Gulfstream jet and the M1A1 Abrams tank largely dodged the worst of the COVID-19 disruptions. In March, the General Dynamics board agreed to hike the quarterly dividend, the 24th consecutive annual increase, even as the company suffered a sharp decline in operating profit on reduced deliveries of its G650 aircraft. But new orders\u2014including a $9.5 billion contract to build Columbia-class submarines\u2014and a record $89.5 billion order backlog point to strong growth potential.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:14723,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:16777215},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\">The company behind the Gulfstream jet and the M1A1 Abrams tank largely dodged the worst of the COVID-19 disruptions. In March, the General Dynamics board agreed to hike the quarterly dividend, the 24th consecutive annual increase, even as the company suffered a sharp decline in operating profit on reduced deliveries of its G650 aircraft. But new orders\u2014including a $9.5 billion contract to build Columbia-class submarines\u2014and a record $89.5 billion order backlog point to strong growth potential.</span>",
